session:pr748Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Dag noticed the current SERVICE-federation error messages (ExecError::ServiceDenied/ServiceNotImplemented) and NetworkPolicy::Allow's doc comment all pointed at issue #51, which is closed -- #51 only tracked the short-term fix (turning a silent empty-result footgun into an explicit error, landed mid-2026), not the actual federation implementation; its closing comment said full federation was 'tracked as a future enhancement' but no live issue for that enhancement was ever filed, so the link was a dead end. Investigated the surrounding NetworkPolicy framework (epic #117, closed) and confirmed SERVICE is genuinely the one unfinished sibling of LOAD (#119, implemented) and JSON-LD @import (#82, implemented) under Allow mode -- both of those already do real HTTP fetches with SSRF hardening (#135) that SERVICE's implementation can and should reuse rather than inventing a second code path. Wrote docs/plans/SPARQL_FEDERATION_PLAN.md covering the actual design gaps found by reading the code directly: no AST->SPARQL-text serializer exists for re-emitting a SERVICE sub-pattern as a request body, no SPARQL-results-JSON reader exists (sparql_json.rs only writes that format), and -- the trickiest part -- execute()/execute_with_base() are fully synchronous and called from both a non-tokio CLI and async axum handlers, so a federation implementation can't just do a blocking HTTP call inline without either stalling the runtime or forking a second async execution path. Filed the epic (#741) and five sub-issues (#742-746) breaking exactly that design into independently landable pieces, mirroring how LOAD's own async pre-resolution already works in the codebase. Also filed #747 (a separate, smaller request made in the same conversation: SPARQL's undeclared-prefix parse error, made correct by #389, still doesn't name which prefix was wrong -- unlike turtle_parser's equivalent message for SPARQL Update) under the existing error-handling epic #453. This PR itself only repoints the dead #51 references to #741 and adds the plan/issues -- no behavior change; implementing real forwarding is #741's sub-issues' job." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:748 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr748Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr748 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr748Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Recommended a 'pre-resolve, don't inline' approach for the eventual federation implementation (#744): walk the WHERE clause for SERVICE clauses and resolve them all via async HTTP from the caller's async context before invoking the synchronous executor, passing it a pre-fetched results map, rather than making execute()/execute_with_base() async." ;
    agp:alternative "Making execute()/execute_with_base() themselves async fn was considered and rejected for this plan: both are called synchronously today from the CLI (no tokio runtime present) and from deep inside the evaluator's recursive eval_components call tree, so turning them async would force every caller and every internal helper function to become async too ('async fn virus'), for a feature (remote HTTP fetch) that only actually needs to happen once per SERVICE clause, before the rest of evaluation runs." .
